WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
Curl a heavy bag up towards your shoulder.

2
00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:06.480
Your biceps shortens and
thickens as it works.

3
00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:09.650
A muscle exerts force only by contracting.

4
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.760
It pulls.

5
00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.400
It never pushes.

6
00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:16.200
Yet a moment later, the same arm
can reach straight out again.

7
00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:21.280
So if a muscle can only pull, how
does a bent arm ever straighten again?

8
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.380
In this mission, you'll
see your arm as a lever:

9
00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:28.440
the elbow is the fulcrum, and
the muscle's pull is the effort.

10
00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:32.370
Then you'll see how tendons,
strong and almost unstretchable,

11
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.210
carry each muscle's pull to the bone.

12
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:38.890
Your mission: explain how a
bent arm straightens again,

13
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.750
when muscles can only pull.
